      "card_ids": ["C20"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Multiple human reference contexts report absolute or estimated oral bioavailability well below 20%: olcegepant %F<1 (C14), DX-9065a F=2–3% and 2.8±1.5% (C03, C06), astemizole 3% (C15), saquinavir 4% (C13), melagatran 3–7% (C12), and emixustat low (C17).",
      "card_ids": ["C14", "C03", "C06", "C15", "C13", "C12", "C17"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "New L2 records add further sub-20% animal F values for related low-bioavailability contexts: emixustat 18.4% in monkeys and 5.2% in rats (C23, C26), compound 56a 19% in dogs (C28), DX-9065a 5–12% in baboons (C31), saquinavir 2.0–4.3% in rats (C24), and olcegepant <1% in rats (C32).",
      "card_ids": ["C23", "C26", "C28", "C31", "C24", "C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only high animal F values in the new L2 set (FK3453 71.3–93.4% in dogs, C18/C21) are species-specific and do not override the human low-F outcome for FK3453 (C01/C08); they are not evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C18", "C21", "C01", "C08"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C22's qualitative statement that olcegepant was 'orally available' is contradicted by direct low-F measurements (C14, C32) and does not provide affirmative F>=20% evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C22", "C14", "C32"]
    }
  ],
