  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct human absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query is supplied; C20 is a monkey Fpod value for compound 4p, and its identity with the query is inferred from the matching pyrazolopyrimidine acrylamide scaffold.",
    "No experimental solubility, permeability, or first-pass metabolism data for the query are supplied; high logP/logD and primary aromatic amine are proxies.",
    "The reference contexts are structurally diverse and none is a close analog of the query; transfer is indirect.",
    "The query's fasted-state condition is not explicitly matched in most reference cards; C20 formulation includes Cremophor/DMSO, which may alter absorption."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is a lipophilic, poorly soluble pyrazolopyrimidine acrylamide (ibrutinib-like). C20 reports an absolute Fpod of 10% for compound 4p with the same core, below the 20% threshold. All transferable human reference contexts report low F (typically <10%), and new L2 animal values are also below 20%. No affirmative high-F evidence for the query is present; the only high animal F values (FK3453 in dogs) are species-specific and not query evidence. Therefore F<20% is better supported."
}

